-- src:76 | (9) Where subsection (8) applies—
-- src:77 | (a) if P does the act in operating an account or accounts, the funds in the account or accounts immediately after the act are assumed to include the relevant criminal property, and
-- src:78 | (b) if P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client, such of that property as is held by P immediately after the act is assumed to include the relevant criminal property.
@ref s 328(9) (src:76-78)
GIVEN `subsection (8) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does the act in operating an account or accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 328(9) the funds or property immediately after the act are assumed to include the relevant criminal property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (8) applies` AND (`P does the act in operating an account or accounts` OR `P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where subsection (8) applies" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')

-- src:45 | (1) A person commits an offence if he enters into or becomes concerned in an arrangement which he knows or suspects facilitates (by whatever means) the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property by or on behalf of another person.
-- src:46 | (2) But a person does not commit such an offence if—
@ref s 328(1) (src:45-46)
GIVEN `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the act of subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure and exemption facts`
      overseas IS A `Overseas conduct facts`
      account IS A `Account facts`
      termination IS A `Termination facts`
      mixed IS A `Mixed funds facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 328(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the act of subsection (1)` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he enters into or becomes concerned in an arrangement which he knows or suspects facilitates" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the offence is of "criminal property", which s 340(3) defines with "Property is criminal property if" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 328(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse or the enforcement of the law applies` disclosure THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a person does not commit such an offence if"
        IF `s 328(3) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` overseas THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nor does a person commit an offence under subsection (1) if"
        IF `s 328(5) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` account THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `s 328(6) the exception for acts that end a business relationship applies` termination THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `s 328(8) the exception for mixed funds applies` mixed THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "criminal property"; whether the property is criminal property is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 328(1) (src:45)
GIVEN `the answer under section 328(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 328(1) the person must not enter into or become concerned in an arrangement which facilitates the use of criminal property` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 328(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `enter into or become concerned in an arrangement which facilitates the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 328(1): the person entered into or became concerned in an arrangement which he knew or suspected facilitates the acquisition, retention, use or control of criminal property"

§§ `s 329: acquisition, use and possession`

-- src:81 | (a) acquires criminal property;
-- src:82 | (b) uses criminal property;
-- src:83 | (c) has possession of criminal property.
@ref s 329(1) (src:81-83)
GIVEN act IS A `Act in section 329(1)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(1) the act is one of those listed` MEANS
    NOT (act EQUALS `another act`)

-- src:85 | (a) he makes an authorised disclosure under section 338 and (if the disclosure is made before he does the act mentioned in subsection (1)) he has the appropriate consent;
-- src:86 | (b) he intended to make such a disclosure but had a reasonable excuse for not doing so;
-- src:87 | (c) he acquired or used or had possession of the property for adequate consideration;
-- src:88 | (d) the act he does is done in carrying out a function he has relating to the enforcement of any provision of this Act or of any other enactment relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct.
@ref s 329(2) (src:85-88)
GIVEN f IS A `Disclosure and exemption facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse, adequate consideration or the enforcement of the law applies` MEANS
        (   f's `he makes an authorised disclosure under section 338`
         AND (   (NOT f's `the disclosure is made before he does the act mentioned in subsection (1)`)
              OR f's `he has the appropriate consent`))
     OR (f's `he intended to make such a disclosure` AND f's `he had a reasonable excuse for not doing so`)
     OR f's `he acquired or used or had possession of the property for adequate consideration`
     OR f's `the act is done in carrying out a function he has relating to the enforcement of any provision of this Act or of any other enactment relating to criminal conduct or benefit from criminal conduct`

-- src:90 | (a) he knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the relevant criminal conduct occurred in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom, and
-- src:91 | (b) the relevant criminal conduct—
-- src:92 | (i) was not, at the time it occurred, unlawful under the criminal law then applying in that country or territory, and
-- src:93 | (ii) is not of a description prescribed by an order made by the Secretary of State.
@ref s 329(2A) (src:90-93)
GIVEN f IS A `Overseas conduct facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` MEANS
        f's `he knows, or believes on reasonable grounds, that the relevant criminal conduct occurred in a particular country or territory outside the United Kingdom`
    AND f's `the relevant criminal conduct was not, at the time it occurred, unlawful under the criminal law then applying in that country or territory`
    AND (NOT f's `the relevant criminal conduct is of a description prescribed by an order made by the Secretary of State`)

-- src:94 | (2B) In subsection (2A) “ the relevant criminal conduct ” is the criminal conduct by reference to which the property concerned is criminal property.
@ref s 329(2B) (src:94)
GIVEN `it is the criminal conduct by reference to which the property concerned is criminal property` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(2B) the conduct is the relevant criminal conduct` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the criminal conduct by reference to which the property concerned is criminal property` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“the relevant criminal conduct” is the criminal conduct by reference to which the property concerned is criminal property"

-- src:95 | (2C) A deposit-taking body , electronic money institution or payment institution that does an act mentioned in subsection (1) does not commit an offence under that subsection if—
-- src:96 | (a) it does the act in operating an account maintained with it, and
-- src:97 | (b) the value of the criminal property concerned is less than the threshold amount determined under section 339A for the act.
@ref s 329(2C) (src:95-97)
GIVEN f IS A `Account facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(2C) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` MEANS
        f's `it is a deposit-taking body, electronic money institution or payment institution`
    AND f's `it does the act in operating an account maintained with it`
    AND f's `the value of the criminal property concerned, in pounds` LESS THAN f's `the threshold amount determined under section 339A for the act, in pounds`

-- src:98 | (2D) A person (“P”) who does an act mentioned in subsection (1) does not commit an offence under that subsection if—
-- src:99 | (a) P is carrying on business in the regulated sector that is not excluded business,
-- src:100 | (b) P does the act, in the course of that business—
-- src:101 | (i) in transferring or handing over to the customer or client property of, or owing to, a customer or client, and
-- src:102 | (ii) for the purposes of the termination of P’s business relationship with the customer or client,
-- src:103 | (c) the total value of the criminal property so transferred or handed over to the customer or client by P for those purposes is less than the threshold amount determined under section 339A for the act, and
-- src:104 | (d) before the act is done, P has complied with the customer due diligence duties.
@ref s 329(2D) (src:98-104)
GIVEN f IS A `Termination facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(2D) the exception for acts that end a business relationship applies` MEANS
        f's `P is carrying on business in the regulated sector`
    AND (NOT f's `the business is excluded business (of a description specified in regulations made by the Secretary of State)`)
    AND f's `P does the act in transferring or handing over to a customer or client money or other property of, or owing to, the customer or client (including to another person at the direction of the customer or client)`
    AND f's `for the purposes of the termination of P's business relationship with the customer or client`
    AND f's `the total value of the criminal property so transferred or handed over, in pounds` LESS THAN f's `the threshold amount determined under section 339A for the act, in pounds`
    AND f's `before the act is done, P has complied with the customer due diligence duties (all duties imposed on P in relation to the customer or client by regulation 28(2), (3), (3A), (4), (8) or (10) of the Money Laundering, Terrorist Financing and Transfer of Funds (Information on the Payer) Regulations 2017)`

-- s 329(2E) says what "excluded" business, a transfer "to the customer or client" and "customer due diligence duties" mean for (2D); each is an input of the rule above (see s 327(2E)).

-- src:109 | (2F) A person (“P”) who does an act mentioned in subsection (1) does not commit an offence under that subsection if—
-- src:110 | (a) P is carrying on business in the regulated sector,
-- src:111 | (b) P does the act in the course of that business, on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or accounts maintained with P or in connection with holding any property for the customer or client,
-- src:112 | (c) at the time of the act, P knows or suspects that part but not all of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, is criminal property (“the relevant criminal property”),
-- src:113 | (d) it is not possible, at the time the act takes place, to identify the part of the funds or property that is the relevant criminal property, and
-- src:114 | (e) the value of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, is not, as a direct or indirect result of the act, less than the value of the relevant criminal property at the time of the act.
@ref s 329(2F) (src:109-114)
GIVEN f IS A `Mixed funds facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 329(2F) the exception for mixed funds applies` MEANS
        f's `P is carrying on business in the regulated sector`
    AND f's `P does the act in the course of that business, on behalf of a customer or client, in operating an account or accounts maintained with P or in connection with holding any property for the customer or client`
    AND f's `at the time of the act, P knows or suspects that part but not all of the funds or property is criminal property`
    AND f's `it is not possible, at the time the act takes place, to identify the part of the funds or property that is the relevant criminal property`
    AND f's `the value of the funds in the account or accounts, or of the property so held, after the act, in pounds` AT LEAST f's `the value of the relevant criminal property at the time of the act, in pounds`

-- src:115 | (2G) Where subsection (2F) applies—
-- src:116 | (a) if P does the act in operating an account or accounts, the funds in the account or accounts immediately after the act are assumed to include the relevant criminal property, and
-- src:117 | (b) if P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client, such of that property as is held by P immediately after the act is assumed to include the relevant criminal property.
@ref s 329(2G) (src:115-117)
GIVEN `subsection (2F) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does the act in operating an account or accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(2G) the funds or property immediately after the act are assumed to include the relevant criminal property` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection (2F) applies` AND (`P does the act in operating an account or accounts` OR `P does the act in connection with holding any property for the customer or client`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where subsection (2F) applies" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (b): a 'where' condition not met is the text's no, like 'if')

-- s 329(3): inadequate consideration.  (a) acquires for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the property;
-- (b) uses or has possession for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the use or possession;
-- (c) the provision of goods or services which he knows or suspects may help another to carry out criminal conduct is not consideration.
-- "Significantly less" has no number; the person states whether it is.
-- src:118 | (3) For the purposes of this section—
-- src:119 | (a) a person acquires property for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the property;
-- src:120 | (b) a person uses or has possession of property for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the use or possession;
-- src:121 | (c) the provision by a person of goods or services which he knows or suspects may help another to carry out criminal conduct is not consideration.
@ref s 329(3) (src:118-121)
DECLARE `Kind of act for the consideration test` IS ONE OF
    `acquires the property`
    `uses or has possession of the property`

GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of act for the consideration test`
      `the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the use or possession` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(3)(a) and (b) the consideration is inadequate` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `acquires the property` THEN IF `the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the property` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person acquires property for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the property" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `uses or has possession of the property` THEN IF `the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the use or possession` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person uses or has possession of property for inadequate consideration if the value of the consideration is significantly less than the value of the use or possession" (marginal reading (a))

@ref s 329(3)(c) (src:121)
GIVEN `it is the provision by a person of goods or services which he knows or suspects may help another to carry out criminal conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(3)(c) the provision of goods or services is consideration` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is the provision by a person of goods or services which he knows or suspects may help another to carry out criminal conduct` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the provision by a person of goods or services which he knows or suspects may help another to carry out criminal conduct is not consideration"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is about the provision of goods or services the person knows or suspects may help another carry out criminal conduct

-- src:80 | (1) A person commits an offence if he—
-- src:81 | (a) acquires criminal property;
-- src:82 | (b) uses criminal property;
-- src:83 | (c) has possession of criminal property.
@ref s 329(1) (src:80-83)
GIVEN `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      act IS A `Act in section 329(1)`
      disclosure IS A `Disclosure and exemption facts`
      overseas IS A `Overseas conduct facts`
      account IS A `Account facts`
      termination IS A `Termination facts`
      mixed IS A `Mixed funds facts`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 329(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 329(1) the act is one of those listed` act THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A person commits an offence if he (a) acquires criminal property; (b) uses criminal property; (c) has possession of criminal property" (a failed "if" read as the text's no: marginal reading (a))
        IF `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` EQUALS JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the offence is of "criminal property", which s 340(3) defines with "Property is criminal property if" (marginal reading (a))
        IF `s 329(2) the exception for a disclosure, an excuse, adequate consideration or the enforcement of the law applies` disclosure THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "But a person does not commit such an offence if"
        IF `s 329(2A) the exception for conduct lawful abroad applies` overseas THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nor does a person commit an offence under subsection (1) if"
        IF `s 329(2C) the exception for acts in operating an account applies` account THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `s 329(2D) the exception for acts that end a business relationship applies` termination THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `s 329(2F) the exception for mixed funds applies` mixed THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not commit an offence under that subsection if"
        IF `the answer under section 340(3): the property is criminal property` EQUALS NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is of "criminal property"; whether the property is criminal property is not answered
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@ref s 329(1) (src:80-83)
GIVEN `the answer under section 329(1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party under Part 7` `Act under Part 7`
`s 329(1) the person must not acquire, use or have possession of criminal property` MEANS
    IF `the answer under section 329(1)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN FULFILLED
    ELSE PARTY `the person`
         SHANT `acquire, use or have possession of criminal property`
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `the person` BECAUSE "s 329(1): criminal property was acquired, used or possessed"

§§ `s 334: penalties`

-- src:331 | (1) A person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329 is liable—
-- src:332 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both, or
-- src:333 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 14 years or to a fine or to both.
@ref s 334(1) (src:331-333)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of being convicted`
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
`s 334(1) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 327, 328 or 329` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 6, `ceiling of the fine` IS `the statutory maximum`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 168, `ceiling of the fine` IS `a fine with no ceiling stated`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE

-- src:334 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331or 332 is liable—
-- src:335 | (a) on summary conviction, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum or to both, or
-- src:336 | (b) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding five years or to a fine or to both.
@ref s 334(2) (src:334-336)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of being convicted`
GIVETH A `Penalty ceiling`
`s 334(2) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 330, 331 or 332` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 6, `ceiling of the fine` IS `the statutory maximum`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN `Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 60, `ceiling of the fine` IS `a fine with no ceiling stated`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS TRUE

-- src:337 | (3) A person guilty of an offence under section 339(1A) is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale.
@ref s 334(3) (src:337)
GIVEN way IS A `Way of being convicted`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Penalty ceiling`
`s 334(3) the most that can be imposed on a person guilty of an offence under section 339(1A)` MEANS
    CONSIDER way
    WHEN `on summary conviction` THEN JUST (`Penalty ceiling` WITH `months of imprisonment` IS 0, `ceiling of the fine` IS `level 5 on the standard scale`, `imprisonment and a fine may both be imposed` IS FALSE)
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says the person "is liable on summary conviction to a fine not exceeding level 5 on the standard scale" and says nothing of conviction on indictment
